   "signature": "void r4d_ar_oneshot_2rank_exact(long peer_scratch, long my_scratch, long peer_flags, long my_flags, long seq_ctrs, long slot_stride16, long inp, long out, long n_elem, long dtype, long stream, long nblocks, long nthreads, long drain, long acq, long stage)",
   "needs": "both cards in ONE process (a thread per rank, hipDeviceEnablePeerAccess, raw peer pointers) or IPC handles from r4d_ar_ipc_alloc; scratch double-buffered by parity, per-block flags, seq_ctrs = 2 * r4d_ar_max_blocks() zeroed words; both ranks launch in lockstep; dtype 0/1/2 = bf16/fp16/fp32. Plugin-row tunable defaults: ar_oneshot_2rank_exact nblocks 0 (library rule), nthreads 1024, drain 3, acq 0; ar_oneshot_2rank_exact_lane nblocks 8, nthreads 256 (plugin-rows-rad13.txt). The plain entries THROW std::runtime_error on a HIP error, which aborts the process through ctypes: use the plugin rows, whose entry wraps every call (r4d_ar_entry.hip R4D_TRY -> RAD_E_DEVICE) and which need their init/fini hooks.",
