   "needs": "the head stored as IQR trellis-coded width classes, produced by the vendor converter (rad-convert, not built here). Our checkpoint's lm_head is BF16 248320 x 5120, so the like-for-like vendor row is r4d_logits_gemm_bf16(a, w, c, M, K, N, a_ld, c_ld, stream): bf16 row-major weight, f32 output, K % 8 == 0 (prototype is in PROTOS). r4d_logits_gemm_fp8 wants rows of K codes + K/128 bf16 scales padded to 16 bytes (5200 bytes at K = 5120).",
   "our_baseline": "the server's lm_head F.linear over the rank's vocabulary shard"
